---
import { useTranslatedPath } from '../../i18n/utils';
import type { SupportedLanguage } from '../../i18n/ui';

interface Props {
  lang?: SupportedLanguage;
}

const { lang = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const translatePath = useTranslatedPath(lang);
---

<!-- Blog Post Content -->
<section class="pt-16 md:pt-20 pb-12">
  <div class="container blog-article">
    <div class="">
      <span class="mono-eyebrow mb-3">Creative Applications</span>
      <h1 class="mb-6 text-xl md:text-2xl lg:text-4xl">
        Top 5 Creative Uses for Extracted Video Frames in Design Projects
      </h1>
      <p class="body-md max-w-[600px] mb-4">
        From mood boards to digital art, explore innovative ways to
        incorporate video frames into your creative workflow and design
        projects.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="prose mx-auto mb-12">
      <p>
        Video is a rich source of visual inspiration, offering dynamic
        compositions, unique lighting situations, and candid moments that
        are difficult to replicate through traditional photography or
        illustration. By extracting frames from videos, designers and
        artists can tap into this wealth of visual material to enhance their
        creative projects in surprising and innovative ways.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our client-side video to image converter makes it easy to harvest
        these visual gems, giving you access to authentic, spontaneous
        moments that can elevate your design work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Creative Use Cases -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="heading-lg mb-4">Top 5 Creative Applications</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <!-- Mood Boards -->
        <article
          class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow p-6"
        >
          <span class="blog-card-meta mb-3 inline-block"
            >Concept Development</span
          >
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">1. Dynamic Mood Boards</h3>
          <p class="body-md mb-4">
            Create rich, evocative mood boards by extracting frames that
            capture specific lighting, color palettes, or emotional tones
            from cinematography.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="body-sm font-semibold">How to use:</p>
            <ul
              class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 space-y-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]"
            >
              <li>Extract color palette inspiration</li>
              <li>Capture cinematic lighting setups</li>
              <li>Gather textural references</li>
              <li>Establish emotional tone for branding</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Motion Reference -->
        <article
          class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow p-6"
        >
          <span class="blog-card-meta mb-3 inline-block"
            >Animation & UI</span
          >
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">2. Animation Reference Sequences</h3>
          <p class="body-md mb-4">
            Extract sequential frames using interval mode to study natural
            motion, timing, and weight distribution for 2D/3D animation and
            UI motion design.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="body-sm font-semibold">How to use:</p>
            <ul
              class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 space-y-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]"
            >
              <li>Study natural human locomotion</li>
              <li>Analyze secondary motion</li>
              <li>Reference squash and stretch</li>
              <li>Create realistic UI transitions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Digital Collages -->
        <article
          class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow p-6"
        >
          <span class="blog-card-meta mb-3 inline-block"
            >Mixed Media</span
          >
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">3. High-Res Digital Collages</h3>
          <p class="body-md mb-4">
            Extract lossless PNG frames to use as raw source material for
            surreal digital collages, poster designs, and editorial
            illustrations.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="body-sm font-semibold">How to use:</p>
            <ul
              class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 space-y-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]"
            >
              <li>Layer candid human expressions</li>
              <li>Isolate interesting backgrounds</li>
              <li>Blend unexpected textures</li>
              <li>Construct visual narratives</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Social Media Graphics -->
        <article
          class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow p-6"
        >
          <span class="blog-card-meta mb-3 inline-block"
            >Marketing</span
          >
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">4. Custom Video Thumbnails</h3>
          <p class="body-md mb-4">
            Capture the exact peak frame of emotional impact or action to
            design custom, high-converting thumbnails for YouTube and social
            media.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="body-sm font-semibold">How to use:</p>
            <ul
              class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 space-y-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]"
            >
              <li>Find zero-blur peak moments</li>
              <li>Extract hero expressions</li>
              <li>Overlay branding and typography</li>
              <li>A/B test different thumbnail styles</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Texture & Asset Harvesting -->
        <article
          class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow p-6 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-2"
        >
          <span class="blog-card-meta mb-3 inline-block"
            >3D & Shading</span
          >
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">5. Real-world Texture Harvesting</h3>
          <p class="body-md mb-4">
            Extract individual frames from 4K/8K nature footage or street
            videos to isolate organic textures like water reflections, smoke
            patterns, and weathered surfaces.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="body-sm font-semibold">How to use:</p>
            <ul
              class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 space-y-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]"
            >
              <li>Harvest seamless organic textures</li>
              <li>Sample realistic lens flares and light leaks</li>
              <li>Create roughness and displacement maps</li>
              <li>Build reference libraries for 3D shaders</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Best Practices for Designers -->
    <section class="mb-12 bg-[var(--color-canvas-elevated)] p-6 rounded-lg">
      <h2 class="heading-lg mb-4">Best Practices for Designers</h2>
      <div class="prose mx-auto">
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-4 pl-6">
          <li>
            <h3 class="heading-md mb-2">Always Export in PNG for Design Work</h3>
            <p>
              When frames will undergo further editing in Photoshop, Figma, or
              Affinity Designer, lossless PNG is critical to prevent
              compression artifacts.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3 class="heading-md mb-2">Utilize Smart Scene Detection for Batch Work</h3>
            <p>
              When dealing with long video files, use our AI-powered scene
              detection to avoid sorting through thousands of redundant frames.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3 class="heading-md mb-2">Check Source Resolution First</h3>
            <p>
              For print or high-res projects, source your video from 4K or 1080p
              footage to ensure the extracted frame has sufficient pixel
              density.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="heading-lg mb-4">Conclusion</h2>
      <div class="prose mx-auto">
        <p>
          Video frames are more than just stopped footage—they are versatile,
          spontaneous design assets that can give your creative work a unique
          competitive edge.
        </p>
        <p>
          With our 100% private, client-side converter, you can harvest
          high-quality frames freely without worrying about cloud upload
          delays or subscription paywalls.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back to Blogs -->
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <a href={translatePath('/blogs')} class="btn-ghost inline-flex items-center">
        <svg
          class="ml-2 w-4 h-4"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
        >
          <path d="M19 12H5M12 5l-7 7 7 7"></path>
        </svg>
        Back to Blogs
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
